            "height": 86.09271523178808,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><strong>Domestic Policy and the \"Jamahiriya\" System</strong><br>\nGaddafi introduced the \"Jamahiriya,\" or \"state of the masses,\" in Libya, which he claimed was a form of direct democracy, though in practice it was considered authoritarian, with power concentrated in his hands.</p>\n\n<p><strong>c1</strong><br>\nEarly Life and Education</p>\n\n<p><strong>Andy Warhol was born Andrew Warhola in 1928 in Pittsburgh, Pennsylvania, to Slovakian immigrant parents. He graduated from the Carnegie Institute of Technology in 1949 with a degree in pictorial design, which laid the groundwork for his later foray into fine art after a successful career as a commercial illustrator in New York.</strong><br>\nBreakthrough in Pop Art</p>\n"
              },
              "metadata": {
                "contentType": "Text",
                "license": "U",
                "title": "Unbenannt: Text",
